item(6,9,'P000015','claim','Support of a finite Radon measure',
    r'''The closing sentence says that one cannot define the support of arbitrary Radon measures after dropping local compactness.''',
    r'''For a finite positive Radon Borel measure \(\mu\) on a Hausdorff space \(X\), with inner compact regularity on every Borel set, define \(\operatorname{supp}\mu=X\setminus\bigcup\{U\subset X:U\text{ open},\mu(U)=0\}\). This is closed and has full measure. Every compact subset of its complement has a finite cover by null open sets and hence measure zero; inner compact regularity gives \(\mu(X\setminus\operatorname{supp}\mu)=0\). Local compactness is not needed for this conclusion.''',
    'E',
    r'''The finite Hausdorff Radon framework is the one used in \citet{courrege1963mesures}. The compact-cover argument above is an editorial check of this sentence, not a claimed quotation from a numbered theorem. The notebook’s exception does not hold under the hypotheses fixed in this record.''',
    'Support exists and is a closed set of full measure in the stated setting. A different, unstated convention for generalized or nonfinite measures cannot be inferred from this sentence.',
    refs=['courrege1963mesures'],literal='false as written',match='partial',verification='indirect',
    reconstruction='The support definition and compact-cover proof are standard editorial clarification of an otherwise omitted source assertion.')
